This project includes a modified nonlinear DAGMA implementation and the
LocallyConnected layer from DAGMA by Kevin Bello, Bryon Aragam and Pradeep
Ravikumar, distributed under the Apache License 2.0.
https://github.com/kevinsbello/dagma

Modifications include adaptive per-edge regularization, optimization diagnostics,
and a standalone estimator interface.

DAGMA: Learning DAGs via M-matrices and a Log-Determinant Acyclicity
Characterization. NeurIPS 2022.

SCORE ordering follows Rolland et al., Score Matching Enables Causal Discovery
of Nonlinear Additive Noise Models. ICML 2022.
Stein estimation includes SteinMixin and kernel_width adapted from dodiscover
(PyWhy), commit 6e64456198a5b66e515f250a8f4b143ebc31c9a6.
Source files: dodiscover/toporder/_base.py and dodiscover/toporder/utils.py.
